<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="global_financial_tension::yield_volatility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating tech geopolitics (sanctions, export controls, sudden corporate delistings) forces rapid sectoral repricing and risk-reassessment by fixed-income investors, producing abrupt swings in credit spreads and government bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::maritime_security_commit" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">A spike in tech-geopolitical tension prompts the US and regional partners to expand naval patrols, convoy escorts and allied presence to deter retaliation or interdiction tied to technology disputes, directly raising aggregate maritime security commitments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::shipping_insurance_premi" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened tech rivalry increases the incidence and perceived risk of state or proxy cyber/kinetic attacks on maritime logistics and insurers' exposure, leading underwriters to raise war‑risk and political‑risk premiums for Gulf transits.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::supply_disruption_risk" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising tech tensions increase incentives for state and proxy actors to use maritime harassment, strikes on shipping or infrastructure, and asymmetric measures as leverage, directly raising the probability and expected severity of energy‑supply disruptions from the region.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_stringency" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising tech geopolitical tension prompts governments to expand export controls and coordinated sanction lists that explicitly target dual‑use AI/semiconductor suppliers and financial facilitators connected to Russia, increasing overall sanctions stringency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="us_trade_protectionism::tariff_policy_uncertaint" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Spikes in tech geopolitical tension prompt ad hoc export controls, sanctions and tariff threat statements from policymakers and regulators, directly increasing unpredictability about upcoming tariff decisions and enforcement.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_trade_protectionism</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" target="us_trade_protectionism::trade_barrier_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising geopolitical competition over AI/tech leads governments to enact concrete measures—tariffs, formal export controls, investment screens and quotas—raising the effective level of trade barriers.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_trade_protectionism</data>
</edge>
