  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher central-bank credibility lowers political pressure to deploy ad‑hoc trade measures to stabilise growth or markets, reducing the frequency and unpredictability of tariff announcements (and the reverse when credibility falls).</data>
