<edge source="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::oil_export_flow_volume" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained rise in long‑term yields raises global borrowing costs and dampens investment and industrial demand, reducing crude demand and thereby lowering oil export volumes transiting Middle East chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::energy_supply_severity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long-term yields raise financing and rollover costs for commodity traders, shipping firms and energy infrastructure projects, prompting reductions in shipments, inventories and investment in alternate routes that increase the likelihood and severity of energy supply disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" target="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher long‑term yields increase the cost of financing multi‑year, capital‑intensive fab builds and depress project NPVs, causing firms to delay, scale back, or cancel semiconductor capacity expansions.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" target="us_trade_protectionism::semiconductor_demand" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long-term yields raise corporate and consumer financing costs and lift discount rates, which dampens capex and demand for durable goods and thereby reduces semiconductor orders over the product-cycle.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_financial_tension</data>
  <data key="d40">us_trade_protectionism</data>
</edge>
