<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::supply_chain_disruption" target="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained supply‑chain disruptions reduce expected long‑run GDP growth and capital demand, lowering the growth component of long‑term yields and putting downward pressure on those yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::supply_chain_disruption" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::maritime_security_commit" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating supply-chain disruptions tied to US protectionist measures push US firms and policymakers to prioritize secure maritime corridors, prompting increased naval escorts, patrols and allied security deployments in the Middle East to protect vulnerable shipments.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::supply_chain_disruption" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.9</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened supply‑chain disruptions increase delays and component shortages for weapons and ammunition production, directly reducing the rate and timeliness of external military aid deliveries to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::supply_chain_disruption" target="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::tech_geopolitical_tensio" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Visible supply interruptions for critical tech components prompt governments to announce defensive industrial measures and export controls and to publicly assign blame, escalating bilateral tech policy friction and geopolitical tension.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
