<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::trade_barrier_level" target="global_financial_tension::long_term_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher trade barriers push up import costs and near‑term inflation expectations and raise term premia as investors price policy uncertainty and protectionism risks, lifting long‑term bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">global_financial_tension</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::trade_barrier_level" target="mideast_iran_us_conflict::shipping_transit_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher US trade barriers quickly reduce bilateral and intermediate goods trade volumes, directly lowering container and bulk ship voyages that transit Middle East chokepoints (Suez/Strait of Hormuz) as shippers curtail shipments and demand for route capacity falls.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">mideast_iran_us_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::trade_barrier_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising tariffs, quotas or other trade barriers raise costs and administrative frictions for cross‑border procurement of weapons and dual‑use components, slowing or lowering the volume of military aid transferred to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_trade_protectionism::trade_barrier_level" target="us_china_ai_tech_rivalry::semiconductor_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher trade barriers and export controls directly block or raise the cost of importing critical fab equipment, precursor chemicals and specialized machinery, forcing delays or cancellations of planned semiconductor fab expansions and reducing near-term installed capacity.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_trade_protectionism</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_ai_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
